  "tagline": "Pure-Rust embedded key-value store: copy-on-write B-trees, ACID, and a stable file format.",
  "description": "redb is an embedded key-value database written entirely in Rust, inspired by LMDB: data lives in copy-on-write B-trees in a single file, readers get MVCC snapshots without blocking the single writer, and commits are crash-safe. Its typed table API (keys and values as Rust types) and savepoints make it feel native in Rust code, and the file format has been declared stable since 1.0, with the 4.x line current in 2026. It is a good default for Rust applications that want a dependency-free, transactional local store; LSM engines like Fjall are better for write-heavy loads.",
